# Workflow: EXECUTION-LOOP

Purpose:
  Define the full autonomous execution machine — the end-to-end flow
  from task creation to completion, including failure handling, loop
  protection, done proof, and knowledge consolidation. This is the
  master diagram that orchestrates TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd,
  LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd, FAILURE-CLASSIFICATION.sdd, DONE-PROOF.sdd,
  LEARNING-GATE.sdd, and HUMAN-DOCS-GATE.sdd.

Owns:
  Execution loop diagram
  Failure handling sub-routine
  Completion verification

FullExecutionMachine:

                  TASK
                    |
              DISCOVER
                    |
          BUILD CONTEXT
                    |
                PLAN
                    |
             PLAN CHECK
                    |
               IMPLEMENT
                    |
                TEST
                    |
             |-- PASS --|
             |          |
            FAIL     REVIEW
             |          |
         CLASSIFY       |
             |          |
        |-- FIXABLE --| |
        |             | |
       FIX      BLOCKED  |
        |               |
        |               |
        | (loop guard check on each cycle)
        |
        TEST
        |
        (PASS returns to REVIEW)

        PASS
          |
    DONE PROOF
          |
      DOCUMENTATION
          |
      KNOWLEDGE GATE
          |
      CONSOLIDATION
          |
        COMPLETE

ExecutionSteps:

  1. TASK
     input: goal, scope, contract (bax EXECUTION-CONTRACT.sdd)
     output: task instance with initial state DISCOVERING

  2. DISCOVER
     state: DISCOVERING
     actions: understand goal, gather requirements, identify stakeholders
     output: task scope, acceptance criteria, dependencies

  3. BUILD CONTEXT
     actions: load @policy.autonomy, @references/, @skills/,
              @decisions/, project architecture
     budget: CONTEXT LEVEL 0→1→2 default (bax runtime/context-builder.sdd)
     output: context manifest, context_confidence rating
     gate: confidence must be sufficient before PLAN (no guessing)

  4. PLAN
     state: PLANNING
     actions: synthesize plan from context, skills, and knowledge
     output: plan with steps, risks, dependencies
     rule: plan is NOT immutable — evolves with new evidence (bax
           EXECUTION-CONTRACT.sdd -> PlanEvolution)

  5. PLAN CHECK
     actions: validate plan against contract (allowed, forbidden,
              approval_required), check autonomy level sufficiency
     gate: approval_required items must get human sign-off
     on_reject: return to PLAN with feedback

  6. IMPLEMENT
     state: IMPLEMENTING
     actions: produce code, tests, documentation within contract scope
     rule: must stay within allowed_actions and allowed scope
     on_violation: CONSTRAINT_FAILURE (escalate immediately)

  7. TEST
     state: TESTING
     sub_state: PASSED | FAILED
     actions: run test suite (unit, integration, BDD)
     PASS -> REVIEW
     FAIL -> CLASSIFY

  8. CLASSIFY
     actions: classify failure (bax FAILURE-CLASSIFICATION.sdd)
     output: failure type + severity + action
     dispatch:
       FIXABLE  -> FIX (consume failure budget)
       BLOCKED  -> BLOCKED state (declare blocker)
       ESCALATE -> ESCALATED state (human intervention)

  9. FIX
     state: FIXING
     actions: apply remedy from failure → action map
     rule: each fix iteration MUST record BEFORE / CHANGE / AFTER
           / RESULT / PROGRESS (bax TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd -> ProgressRule)
     loop_guard: LOOP_SCORE recalculated, guards checked (bax
                 LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd)
       - LOOP_RISK_HIGH -> strategy change required
         (do NOT retry same approach)
     on_fix: return to TEST

  10. REVIEW
      state: REVIEWING
      sub_state: PASS | PASS_WITH_WARNINGS | CHANGES_REQUIRED | BLOCKED | ESCALATE
      actions:
        - correctness check
        - security check
        - architecture check
        - DDD boundaries
        - SOLID, KISS, DRY, YAGNI
        - performance, observability, testability, maintainability
        - project conventions
        - existing skills and decisions
      rule: only EFFECTIVE knowledge applies (bax context/priorities.sdd)
      PASS / PASS_WITH_WARNINGS -> DONE PROOF
      CHANGES_REQUIRED -> FIX -> TEST -> REVIEW
      BLOCKED -> BLOCKED state
      ESCALATE -> ESCALATED state

  11. DONE PROOF
      actions: produce Done Proof (bax DONE-PROOF.sdd)
      gate: ALL dimensions ✓ (requirements, tests, architecture,
            review, documentation)
      FAIL -> return to the failing dimension's stage
      PASS -> DOCUMENTATION

  12. DOCUMENTATION
      state: DOCUMENTING
      actions: generate human docs (bax HUMAN-DOCS-GATE.sdd)
      gate: documentation complete and reviewed

  13. KNOWLEDGE GATE
      state: LEARNING
      actions: classify knowledge (bax LEARNING-GATE.sdd)
      output: promoted skills, updated decisions, new lessons
      gate: at least one knowledge artifact produced (or NO_NEW_KNOWLEDGE
            explicitly justified)

  14. CONSOLIDATION
      actions: collapse runtime trace into persistent knowledge
      rule: 100 events -> 3 decisions + 1 new skill (bax
            EXECUTION-CONTRACT.sdd -> ExecutionSummary)
      output: execution summary, knowledge artifacts

  15. COMPLETE
      state: COMPLETED
      actions: archive task, update task registry, release resources

LoopProtectionIntegration:

  guards run at every TEST -> FIX -> TEST cycle:
    1. max_iterations (from EXECUTION-CONTRACT)
    2. failure_budget (severity-weighted, from ExecUTION-CONTRACT)
    3. no_progress_detection (consecutive no-progress iterations)
    4. duplicate_action_detection (same action + same reasoning)
    5. state_transition_rules (allowed transitions enforced)
    6. human_escalation (6th guard, bax LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd -> Guards)

  LOOP_SCORE recalculated after every cycle iteration.
  LOOP_SCORE >= 60 -> LOOP_RISK_HIGH -> strategy change required.

Rules:

  [EL1] The execution machine starts at TASK and ends at COMPLETE.
  [EL2] Every state transition MUST be recorded in the execution trace.
  [EL3] TEST -> FAIL MUST classify the failure before choosing FIX/FIXABLE.
  [EL4] Context confidence MUST be sufficient before PLAN (no guessing).
  [EL5] Review is embedded in the loop — NOT a post-completion step.
  [EL6] Done Proof is required before DOCUMENTATION — not optional.
  [EL7] Knowledge gate MUST produce at least one artifact OR justify
        NO_NEW_KNOWLEDGE.
  [EL8] Consolidation collapses trace into 3 categories: decisions,
        skills, lessons.
  [EL9] COMPLETED requires Engineering Done, not Functional Done.
  [EL10] LOOP_SCORE >= 60 forces strategy change — AI MUST NOT retry
         the same approach.

